addonsTools.description:
AddonsTools is a set of tools for managing add-ons that are not available in the NVDA Add-ons Store:
Add-on Packager: To create a backup file of an add-on or to send a modified add-on to someone else for testing or use;
Multiple installer: Allows you to select add-ons from a folder and install them all at once;
Create/Restore Backups: Allows you to backup and restore some NVDA settings, such as configurations, profiles and dictionaries;
Add-on Documentation: Allows you to open the documentation file.
Previously this add-on was called addonPackager.

ExcelPlus.description:
The ExcelPlus add-on adds the following features when using Microsoft Excel:
Say the address of the current cell – Alt+W;
Say the column heading of the current cell – Alt+E;
Say the row title of the current cell – Alt+R.
You can change the command in input gestures, in the ExcelPlus section.
You can declare a cell as a header using standard NVDA commands:
Column heading – NVDA+Shift+C;
The line header is NVDA+Shift+R.
